### ===== PREFERENCES =====
# If P-01 returns 409 on the first try, user 1 already has preferences
# from earlier testing. Change pref_user to 10 and start again.
@pref_user = 1

### P-01 create preferences -> expect 201
POST {{base_url}}/api/v1/preferences/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": {{pref_user}},
  "email_enabled": true,
  "sms_enabled": false,
  "push_enabled": true,
  "quiet_hours_enabled": true,
  "quiet_hours_start": "22:00",
  "quiet_hours_end": "07:00",
  "frequency": "realtime"
}

### P-02 create again for same user -> expect 409
POST {{base_url}}/api/v1/preferences/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": {{pref_user}}
}

### P-03 get preferences -> expect 200
GET {{base_url}}/api/v1/preferences/{{pref_user}}

### P-04 get for user that doesn't exist -> expect 404
GET {{base_url}}/api/v1/preferences/999999

### P-05 update -> expect 200, only these fields change
PUT {{base_url}}/api/v1/preferences/{{pref_user}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sms_enabled": true,
  "receive_low_priority": false,
  "digest_enabled": true,
  "frequency": "daily"
}

### P-06 update for user that doesn't exist -> expect 404
PUT {{base_url}}/api/v1/preferences/999999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sms_enabled": true
}

### P-07 create with user_id 0 -> expect 422
POST {{base_url}}/api/v1/preferences/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": 0
}

### P-08 invalid quiet hours -> SHOULD be 422 (see notes)
PUT {{base_url}}/api/v1/preferences/{{pref_user}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quiet_hours_start": "25:99",
  "frequency": "whenever"
}

